"SOURCE/io/include/nexus/io/rtc.h), [public LPTIM](https://github.com/X-Gen-"
"Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/io/include/nexus/io/lptim.h), "
"[Native implementation](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/io/native/rtc_lptim.c), [Native "
"assembly](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/tools/configure/providers/native/bindings.py). {download}`Editable "
"DOT <rtc-lptim-lifecycle.dot>`; implementation link: IO-36. Assess "
"development software evidence separately from main/SDK/candidate/hardware "
"qualification; neither this diagram nor successful rendering establishes "
"those results."

#: ../../../../../tmp/nexus-h743-spi-safe-stop-20261018/docs/assets/diagrams/README.md:3
msgid "本图册保留15类必需视图、两张补充图与本轮 I/O 架构视图 FIG-16， 另加入 IO-24 的 FIG-17/18 目标图源、IO-36 的 FIG-21 Native 装配／生命周期图， 以及 IO-31 的 FIG-22 G474 命名 GPIO 状态／所有权图。FIG-23–26 依次描述 五项有界软件机制的所有权、U575 保留时钟与 Stop2 所有权及状态、 UART TX 复制代理的 kernel 所有权与退出、I3C 核心借用与整总线证明。 FIG-27 另述同一 Stop2 owner 的选定 SRAM4/LPDMA 有限复制及复合退出。主图登记见 {download}`图清单 <diagram-index.csv>`，维护规则见 [图示标准](../../design/documentation-standards.md)。图有精确current/reference/target身份， 不可从图源存在、渲染成功或软件流程推断硬件和外部发布已执行。"
msgstr "This gallery retains 15 required view types, two supplementary figures and the current I/O architecture view FIG-16, together with the IO-24 target diagram sources FIG-17/18, the IO-36 FIG-21 Native assembly/lifecycle diagram, and the IO-31 FIG-22 G474 named GPIO state/ownership diagram. FIG-23–26 respectively describe ownership of five bounded software mechanisms, U575 retained-clock and Stop2 ownership and state, kernel ownership and exit for the copied UART TX broker, and I3C core borrowing and whole-bus proofs. FIG-27 separately describes the same Stop2 owner's selected finite SRAM4/LPDMA copy and compound exit. See the {download}`figure index <diagram-index.csv>` for the main register and the [diagram standards](../../design/documentation-standards.md) for maintenance rules. Each figure has an explicit current/reference/target identity. The existence of diagram sources, successful rendering or a software workflow does not establish that hardware execution or external publication has occurred."

#: ../../../../../tmp/nexus-h743-spi-safe-stop-20261018/docs/assets/diagrams/README.md:16
msgid ""
"当前每张图均提供中英文视图；新增 FIG-17/18 的渲染与审查须分别取得 实际记录。页面按所选语言使用本地SVG。节点、箭头、属性与 "
"范围仍由同一canonical DOT维护；`labels.json`只维护完整标签译文，不能改变拓扑。 "
"各语言DOT/SVG应与原图配对检查；缺失译文、陈旧输出和非法资源使门禁失败。 SVG采用Graphviz "
"Cairo字形路径输出，使离线读者无需安装中文字体；每图附title、 "
"desc和正文alt/caption。生成主机需要锁定Graphviz、Cairo及Noto Sans CJK SC， "
"最终工具身份与自动检查结果由文档交付记录绑定。源码语义、实际浏览器桌面/窄屏/ "
"放大/打印与离线包验收分开记录。原15主图和2补充图保留各自已完成的审查；新增 FIG-16/17/18 "
"的内容、图示和翻译审查状态单独记录，不能从渲染成功推断。浏览器与正式包 验收另按实际执行记录判断，这些状态不建立 HIL 或公开部署资格。"
msgstr ""
"Each current diagram has English and Chinese views. Rendering and review of "
"the additional FIG-17/18 sources require separate actual records. Pages use "
"local SVGs for the selected language. Nodes, arrows, attributes and scope "
"remain maintained in one canonical DOT; `labels.json` contains complete "
"label translations without changing topology. Language DOT/SVG pairs are "
"checked against their source figures; missing translations, stale outputs or"
" invalid resources fail the gate. SVGs use Graphviz Cairo glyph paths so "
"offline readers do not need installed Chinese fonts; each figure has a "
"title, desc and body alt/caption. The generation host requires locked "
"Graphviz, Cairo and Noto Sans CJK SC. Documentation delivery records bind "
"the actual tool identity and automated checks. Source semantics, actual "
"browser desktop/narrow-screen/zoom/print checks and offline-package "
"acceptance are recorded separately. The original 15 main figures and two "
"supplementary figures retain their completed reviews; content, diagram and "
"translation reviews for FIG-16/17/18 are recorded independently and cannot "
"be inferred from successful rendering. Browser and formal-package acceptance"
" follow their actual execution records; these states do not establish HIL or"
" public deployment qualification."

